{"id": "EUVD-2026-104922", "enisaUuid": "88d43827-38ad-375d-9c1e-042a781a44e0", "description": "libexpat 2.7.2 through 2.9.0 contains a denial of service vulnerability because XML_ParserReset zeroes the direct byte count but never offsets tracked heap allocations. Attackers can submit a large XML document so later documents on the same reset parser fail with XML_ERROR_NO_MEMORY until it is recreated.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T10:41:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T16:06:48", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/pull/1431", "https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/blob/a76b1174c1ea52abb639a4c69d52b630a8a106a2/expat/lib/xmlparse.c#L860-L884", "https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/blob/a76b1174c1ea52abb639a4c69d52b630a8a106a2/expat/lib/xmlparse.c#L1560", "https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libexpat-2.7.2-through-2.9.0-denial-of-service-via-xml-parserreset"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-113351", "GHSA-6r6q-9jmv-gg3h"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.47, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7364fa73-7d1e-3e16-b6e8-3204fb5df8bb", "product": {"name": "libexpat", "vendor": {"name": "libexpat project"}}, "product_version": "2.7.2 \u22642.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "aa264b18-4412-3844-ac62-695974c00536", "vendor": {"name": "libexpat"}}], "isExploited": false}